WEBVTT

00:01:28.292 --> 00:01:30.711
The confusion is understandable though—

00:01:30.711 --> 00:01:33.297
the Black Death had several aftershocks,

00:01:33.297 --> 00:01:37.051
including a series of devastating
outbreaks in Western Europe

00:01:37.051 --> 00:01:39.303
during the 17th century.

00:01:39.303 --> 00:01:43.891
This is when the iconic plague doctor
actually emerged on the scene.

00:01:45.017 --> 00:01:47.812
First described in the early 17th century,

00:01:47.812 --> 00:01:51.566
the outfit consisted of a hood 
with crystal eyepieces

00:01:51.566 --> 00:01:55.695
and a beak filled with a pungent 
combination of herbs and compounds.

00:01:56.028 --> 00:01:59.991
This could include cinnamon, pepper,
turpentine,

00:01:59.991 --> 00:02:03.661
roast copper, and powdered viper flesh.